    "result_text": "You can now add clients with a name and email and see them all in one list. `bin/e2e` builds the app and both Playwright tests pass: listing seeded clients, and creating a client.\n\n**About OfficeFloor:** your request asked for an OfficeFloor server, but this repo is a Spring Boot app (CLAUDE.md, `pom.xml`). So I built the server side with standard Spring.\n\n**Database:** `V1__create_client.sql` adds a `client` table with `id`, `name` and `email`.\n\n**Server** (in `net.officefloor.hq.app.client`):\n- `GET /api/clients` returns all clients, ordered by id.\n- `POST /api/clients` creates one. It returns 400 if the name or email is blank or the email isn't valid.\n- I filled in the test setup endpoints in `TestSupportController`. Reset empties the client table and restarts its ids. Seed inserts the given clients with their ids, then sets the next generated id to follow them so new clients can't clash with seeded ones.\n\n**Front end:**\n- A new lazy-loaded Clients page appears in the nav as `nav-clients`.\n- It has a form with field labels and inline error messages. An error message appears if a field is left empty or the email is invalid.\n- Clients show in a table, or a \"No clients yet.\" message when there are none.\n- Every `data-testid` matches the spec.\n\nThe project is on Angular 21, so I used Reactive Forms and `@Injectable({ providedIn: 'root' })`. CLAUDE.md prefers Signal Forms and the `@Service` decorator, but it describes those as Angular v22+.\n\nI didn't add an audit record for client creation, because the spec doesn't ask for one.",
